 causing it to be memorized first. Consequently, adjusting sampling weights to close the generalization gap between classes inevitably widens the memorization gap, and vice versa. 4 Numerical Experiments on Fashion MNIST Model, Training, and Generation. A standard DDPM [ 22 ] was employed on the Fashion MNIST dataset [ 60 ] , with a UNet [ 44 ] serving as the backbone. Each model is trained on a binary subset of Fashion MNIST, pairing the Sneaker class—which exhibits the lowest pixel-wise variance—with the remaining nine classes to yield nine distinct class pairs. Each pair is trained at three Sneaker proportions (25%, 50%, 75%) on 8,000 images. To capture both early and late training dynamics, 32 log-spaced checkpoints are saved per run. At each checkpoint, the DDPM ancestral sampler [ 22 ] is used to generate 500 samples per pair. Further implementation details are deferred to Appendix J.1 . Evaluation. Following [ 61 , 20 , 8 ] , a generated sample 𝒙 c  m{x}_{c} is considered memorized if the distance ratio to its nearest training neighbors satisfies ‖ 𝒙 c − nn 1 ​ ( 𝒙 c ) ‖ 2 ‖ 𝒙 c − nn 2 ​ ( 𝒙 c ) ‖ 2 < 1 3  rac{\| m{x}_{c}-\mathrm{nn}_{1}( m{x}_{c})\|_{2}}{\| m{x}_{c}-\mathrm{nn}_{2}( m{x}_{c})\|_{2}}< rac{1}{3} . The per-class memorization fraction f mem c ​ ( t ) f_{\mathrm{mem}}^{c}(t) is the expected memorization fraction under the data distribution at diffusion time t t . We define the threshold-crossing time t mem c = inf { t : f mem c ​ ( t ) ≥ 1 / 3 } t_{\mathrm{mem}}^{c}=\inf\{t:f_{\mathrm{mem}}^{c}(t)\geq 1/3\} , yielding the Sneaker-partner memorization gap Δ ​ t mem ​ ( c p ) = t mem snk − t mem c p \Delta t_{\mathrm{mem}}(c_{p})=t_{\mathrm{mem}}^{\mathrm{snk}}-t_{\mathrm{mem}}^{c_{p}} . Samples are assigned to classes using dedicated binary ResNet-18 classifiers [ 21 ] (macro F1 > 96.0 % >96.0\% , balanced accuracy > 97.3 % >97.3\% ). Results and Discussion. Figure 5: DDPM memorization gaps on Fashion MNIST. ( a ) Per-class memorization fractions 